{
	// The tests tree's own resolution context.
	//
	// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. bun resolves path aliases from the NEAREST tsconfig walking up from the
	// importing file. Tests currently living under `src` inherit
	// `.svelte-kit/tsconfig.json`, which SvelteKit generates with `$lib`, `$lib/server` and
	// `$lib/contract` in it. A test moved to `tests/` leaves that context entirely, and a probe confirmed
	// the failure is immediate and loud: `Cannot find module '$lib/position-sentence'`. So the aliases have
	// to be re-declared here, once, rather than rewritten into hundreds of relative paths.
	//
	// WHY NOT ADD THESE TO THE ROOT tsconfig INSTEAD. The root config `include`s `src`, so a
	// `$lib` entry there would collide with the one SvelteKit generates for the same files. Scoping them to
	// this tree keeps the two contexts independent.
	//
	// WHY `@encore/test-support` IS DECLARED HERE AND NOWHERE ELSE. It is test-only. Declaring it in the
	// app's vite config would make it resolvable from production source and therefore bundleable, which is
	// exactly the coupling this package exists to avoid. A test gains access to it by MOVING here, which is
	// also what makes "adopt the helper" and "leave the source tree" the same commit.
	// WHY `$routes`, `$setup` AND `$e2e` ARE HERE. `$lib` covers `src/lib` and nothing else, so a test
	// naming a ROUTE handler, the Svelte client setup, or the e2e selector registry had no alias to use
	// and counted `..` hops instead — 31 of them across 30 files, at depths from two to six. A hop count
	// encodes the importing file's distance from its subject, which is the same fragility that left six
	// e2e drivers anchored one hop short of the repo root. These three aliases delete the whole class.
	//
	// They are declared HERE, in the tests-only context, deliberately: `$routes` resolvable from
	// production source would let a component import a route handler, and `$setup`/`$e2e` would make test
	// scaffolding bundleable. The app's own resolution never sees them.
	"extends": "../tsconfig.base.json",
	"compilerOptions": {
		"baseUrl": ".",
		"paths": {
			"@encore/test-support": ["./support/src/index.ts"],
			"@encore/test-support/*": ["./support/src/*.ts"],
			"$lib": ["../src/lib"],
			"$lib/*": ["../src/lib/*"],
			"$lib/server": ["../src/lib/server"],
			"$lib/server/*": ["../src/lib/server/*"],
			"$routes/*": ["../src/routes/*"],
			"$setup/*": ["./setup/*"],
			"$e2e/*": ["./e2e/*"]
		}
	},
	"include": ["**/*.ts", "./support/src/**/*.ts"]
}
